---
title: Pomegranate Molasses Glazed Turkey
servings: 8
prepTime: 20 minutes
cookTime: 2 hours
Rating: 8/10
source: https://catzinthekitchen.com/2014/11/pomegranate-molasses-glazed-turkey.html
tags: Turkey
---

> Estimate for 12-14 lb turkey at 325F is 3-4 hours. A 14-18 lb turkey is 3:45-4:15 hours. (tasteofhome.com)

> Estimate is 13 min/lb at 350F (thekitchn.com), so 15 lb = 3h15m.

> Pom flavor was prominent but not overpowering. Cooked on raised broiler pan, was not done on bottom in 3 hours.

= Turkey =
Preheat oven to 450°F.

Remove gimlets from inside of the @turkey{12-15%lb}.
Rinse turkey inside and out with cold water. Pat dry.

Rub the entire surface of the turkey with @butter{1/2%cup}(unsalted, softened).
Season well inside and out with @salt and @pepper.
Place breast-up on a rack in a #roasting pan{}.

Cook for ~{45%minutes}, and then reduce heat to 350°F.

= Glaze =
While cooking, prepare the glaze in a medium bowl.
Whisk together @pomegranate molasses{14%oz}, @?horseradish{3/4%cup}(optional),
@dijon mustard{3%tbsp}, @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1 1/2%tsp}.
Let sit at room temperature for about 30-45 minutes before using it, allowing the flavors to meld.

= Basting =
After reducing the oven's heat, begin basting the turkey every 15 minutes with the @chicken broth{1.5%cups}(low-sodium), for about another hour.

For the last 15 minutes, baste the turkey with about 3/4 of the pomegranate glaze,
and allow to finish cooking, or until the thigh temperature reaches about 160°F.

Remove from the oven, baste with remaining glaze, and tent with foil,
allowing turkey to rest before carving for about another 15 minutes.

